\end_layout

\begin_deeper
\begin_layout Enumerate
Diodes function by limiting current flow to one direction.
 This effectively rectifies signals below 0V passed through the diode.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Additionally, adding a DC offset to the signal via voltage divider allows
 the diode to function properly.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
After the signal passes through the diode, a low-pass filter is then used
 to filter out the carrier frequency.
 Like high-pass filters, low-pass filters only allow frequencies below 
\begin_inset Formula $f_{cut}$
\end_inset

